Rebased onto main after #32 merged (2025-11-17).

---

## Why

The codebase had accumulated significant boilerplate code across 41+ data classes, services, and utilities. Manual getters/setters, logger declarations, null checks, and verbose collection operations consumed tokens, slowed AI code generation, and made code reviews slower.

**Business drivers:**
- Reduce AI processing costs (fewer tokens)
- Faster AI code generation (clearer patterns)
- Faster code reviews (less boilerplate to review)
- Better developer velocity for future features

## What

Applied comprehensive Lombok annotations and modern Java patterns across entire codebase:

**Lombok adoption:**
- `@Data` on 41 data classes (eliminated ~1,800 lines of getters/setters/toString)
- `@Slf4j` on all services (eliminated manual logger declarations)
- `@RequiredArgsConstructor` on services (eliminated boilerplate constructors)

**Modern Java patterns:**
- `StringUtils.hasText()` for all null/empty string checks (8 locations)
- `Stream.toList()` instead of `.collect(Collectors.toList())` (13 locations)
- `CollectionUtils.isEmpty()` for collection checks (10 locations)

**Standards documentation:**
- Updated CLAUDE.md with comprehensive coding standards
- Extracted POM dependency versions to properties
- Added AI model labeling guidance for autonomous agent tracking

**Bug fix:**
- Fixed LibraryExtended JSON property stability with `@JsonProperty` annotations

## How

**1. Lombok @Data transformation (mcp-857):**
Applied `@Data` to all 41 classes in `sdkextension/data/` package. Lombok generates getters, setters, toString, equals, hashCode at compile time.

**2. Lombok logging & DI (mcp-1jp):**
- Added `@Slf4j` to all services → replaces `private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(...)`  
- Added `@RequiredArgsConstructor` → replaces manual Spring constructors with `final` field injection

**3. Modern Java APIs:**
- `StringUtils.hasText(str)` replaces `str != null && !str.isEmpty()` (better whitespace handling)
- `Stream.toList()` replaces `.collect(Collectors.toList())` (Java 16+ feature)
- `CollectionUtils.isEmpty()` for consistent collection null/empty checks

**4. POM property extraction (mcp-0bt):**
Centralized 7 dependency versions in `<properties>` section for easier upgrades.

**5. CLAUDE.md standards (mcp-ylk):**
Documented all coding standards with concise examples to guide AI code generation.

**6. Bug fix (mcp-j2m):**
Added `@JsonProperty` to LibraryExtended to preserve legacy JSON property names for backwards compatibility.

## Step-by-step Walkthrough

### Core Changes (Data Classes)

**Before (Application.java - 415 lines):**
```java
public class Application {
  private String appId;
  private String name;
  // ... 40 more fields

  public String getAppId() { return appId; }
  public void setAppId(String appId) { this.appId = appId; }
  public String getName() { return name; }
  public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }
  // ... 120 more getter/setter methods
  @Override public String toString() { /* 20 lines */ }
  @Override public boolean equals(Object o) { /* 15 lines */ }
  @Override public int hashCode() { /* 10 lines */ }
}
```

**After (Application.java - ~350 lines):**
```java
@Data
public class Application {
  private String appId;
  private String name;
  // ... 40 more fields
  // All getters/setters/toString/equals/hashCode generated by Lombok
}
```

**Impact:** 41 classes transformed, ~1,800 lines eliminated

### Service Improvements

**Before (AssessService.java):**
```java
@Service
public class AssessService {
  private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(AssessService.class);
  private final String hostName;
  private final String apiKey;
  // ... more fields

  public AssessService(
      @Value("${contrast.host-name}") String hostName,
      @Value("${contrast.api-key}") String apiKey,
      // ... more params
  ) {
    this.hostName = hostName;
    this.apiKey = apiKey;
    // ... more assignments
  }
}
```

**After:**
```java
@Service
@Slf4j
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class AssessService {
  @Value("${contrast.host-name}") private final String hostName;
  @Value("${contrast.api-key}") private final String apiKey;
  // ... more fields
  // Constructor and logger auto-generated by Lombok
}
```

### String Validation

**Before:**
```java
if (sessionMetadataName != null && !sessionMetadataName.isEmpty()) {
  // do something
}
```

**After:**
```java
if (StringUtils.hasText(sessionMetadataName)) {
  // do something  
}
```

**Benefits:** Better whitespace handling, more expressive, fewer tokens

### Collection Operations

**Before:**
```java
List<String> result = stream.collect(Collectors.toList());
if (collection != null && !collection.isEmpty()) { ... }
```

**After:**
```java
List<String> result = stream.toList();
if (!CollectionUtils.isEmpty(collection)) { ... }
```

## Testing

**All tests passing:**
- ✅ **229 unit tests** - 0 failures, 0 errors
- ✅ **26 integration tests** - 0 failures, 0 errors  
- ✅ **Total: 255 tests** - all green

**Test coverage:**
- Added `LoggingAnnotationsTest` - verifies @Slf4j adoption (2 tests)
- Added `StreamToListUsageTest` - verifies .toList() adoption (1 test)
- Added `CollectionGuardTest` - verifies CollectionUtils adoption (1 test)
- Added `LibraryExtendedTest` - verifies JSON property stability (1 test)

**Manual verification:**
- Lombok bytecode generation verified via `mvn clean compile`
- Code formatting verified via `mvn spotless:check`
- All services properly inject dependencies at runtime

## Impact

**Code reduction:**
- **75 files changed:** +2,279 lines, -3,645 lines
- **Net reduction: -1,366 lines** (~8% codebase reduction)
- **Boilerplate eliminated:** ~1,870 lines (getters/setters/constructors/loggers)

**Developer velocity improvements:**
- Less code to review in PRs
- Clearer patterns for AI code generation
- Faster navigation (less boilerplate noise)
- Easier to maintain (centralized version management in POM)

**AI code generation improvements:**
- CLAUDE.md now documents all standards with examples
- AI will follow established patterns automatically
- Fewer tokens to process (cost savings)

